          0 0
          
8)What will be the output of below program?

public class Test {
	int x = 90;
	int y = 60;

	public static void getX() {
		System.out.println(x);
	}
	public void getY() {
		System.out.println(y);
	}
	
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		Test t = new Test();
		t.getX();
		t.getY();
	}
}

a)90 60
b)91 61
c)Compile time error [Can't call static method through object reference]
d)Compile time error [Can't access non-static variable directly from static context]

Answer:(d)Compile time error [Can't access non-static variable directly from static context]

9)What will be the output of below program?

public class Test {
	int x = 90;
	int y = 60;
        void m1(){
         System.out.println(new Test().x); //Line 1
        }
	
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		Test t = new Test();
		t.x; //Line 2
        t.m1(); //Line 3
		System.out.println(t.y);
                
	}
}
 
a) Compile time error [line 1]
b) Compile time error [line 2]
c) Compile time error [line 3]
d) 90 
   90
   60
e) 90
   60

Answer:(b) Compile time error [line 2]

10)What will be the Output of the program ?

public class Think {
	int a = 10;
	int b = 20;

	public void m1(int a, int b) {
		a++;
		a += this.b;
	}

	public static void main(String[] args) {
		Think a1 = new Think();
		a1.m1(a1.a, a1.b);
		Think a2 = new Think();
		a2.a = 30;
		a1.b = 50;
		System.out.println(a2.a + " ....." + a2.b);
	}
}

Answer:30 .....20

Constructor related Mcq...
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1) Which of the following is/are true about constructors in Java?
   a.Constructor name should be same as class name.
   b.If you don't define a constructor for a class, a default parameter less constructor
     is automatically created by the compiler. 
   c.The default constructor calls super() and initializes all instance variables to default 
     value like 0, null.
   d.If we want to call parent class constructor, it must be called in first line of constructor.
A. 1,2 and 3   
B.2  
C. 1  
D. 1,2,3 and 4

Answer:(D)1,2,3 and 4

2) Which of the following modifier is not applicable for constructors? 
	A. private   	
	B. protected  	
	C. public 	
	D. final
	
Answer:(D)final

3) The implicit return type of a constructor is ?
	A. void	
	B. There is no return type 
	C. a class object in which it is defined		
	D. None of these
	
Answer:(B)There is no return type

4) public class Test 
   {   
   }   
   What  is the prototype of the default constructor ?
	A. public Test(void)	
	B. Test() 	
	C. Test(void)	
	D. public Test()

Answer:(D)public Test()

5) Can we define method with same name of class name?
	A. Yes 	B. No
	
Answer:(A)Yes

6) What happens if we add return type to constructor ?
	A. Compile time error 		
	B. Run Time Error
	C. JVM treats that as method	            
	D. None of these
	
Answer:(C)JVM treats that as method

7) Can we declare constructor as private ?
	A. Yes		B. No
	
Answer:(A)Yes

8) What is the default accessibility modifier of a default constructor?
	A. private	
	B. protected
	C. default	
	D. same as class accessibility modifier
	
Answer:(D)same as class accessibility modifier

9)  Can we define a constructor using all four access modifiers:         
    public, protected, default and private?
	A. Yes      	B.No
	
Answer:(A)Yes

10) Choose correct option for the following code
public class ConstructorTest 
{
	public int a = 10;
	public String ConstructorTest(int a)
                   {
		this.a = a;
	}
}
A.	Run time error
B.	No error
C.	Compile time error
D.	10

Answer:(C)Compile time error

